icity prices are low  then you will switch to  the production of a certain chemical  based on electrochemical process  and i think catalysis is at the core of  everything that we have in our daily  life  so if you think about most of the  products that you're using daily  at some point a catalyst was used and  and whether you are you are doing this  with cerebral catalysis through  electrochemistry through biological  catalysis  i think this is something that is really  really  very important for the development of  our society  [Music]  so in the field of co2 electron  reduction there is a very strong link  now to biology there are already  a number of research groups and even  industry interested in using  algae for example as a catalyst and so  there is a lot of interest in combining  also organic and inorganic  systems and using also things that  nature give us  as a electrocatalyst so i believe that  there is a lot of synergy between these  aspects of catalysis  i studied biology and the other level i  mean  of a woman during those studies was much  more than than  men i think it was about 50 percent  but it leveled out a little bit later  then  at the moment i think my at my  university in potsdam  i'm at the biochemistry and biology  department we have 40  female professors so the university is  doing a good job in hiring women so when  i when i  started my career in spain there was not  a big difference between number of  female studying in physics it was 60  male 40 female but this changed when i  moved to the us and this has  dramatically changed when i moved to  germany  so i was the only female professor in  the physics department at the rural  university warhol  when i joined and then when i when i  became a director of the freestyle  institute i was the first female  director in the history  so this is over 100 years so there is a  it is a big change i don't see a  difference between female and male  scientists in terms of you know i always  talk to co